  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since the degree of the trinomial $5{x}^{2}-7x+1$ is $2,$ it is a quadratic trinomial.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since the degree of the trinomial ${x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+x$ is $3,$ it is a cubic trinomial.\n\n- Statement III is true. A trinomial *could be* cubic (see, for example, statement II). \n\n However, a trinomial is *not always* cubic (see, for example, statement I). \n\n So, some trinomials are cubic.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
